          "kind": "user",
          "reference": "user-confirmed"
        }
      ],
      "status": "verified",
      "updatedAt": "2026-08-23T05:36:03Z",
      "value": "Gateway is the HTTP edge and calls typed upstream clients without accessing service storage. Identity owns identity domain behavior and persistence. Knowledge owns document metadata, permissions, publication/public projections, document trash, quotas, outbox, and the temporary legacy document-attachment compatibility surface, but not Yjs binary state or new attachment storage. Attachment owns unified file metadata, multipart upload lifecycle, private object-storage access, malware scan state, attachment references, and attachment trash lifecycle in the PostgreSQL attachment schema. Collaboration is the Rust Volo Thrift and WebSocket/Yrs service; it owns collaboration state in its PostgreSQL schema and rechecks document access through Knowledge RPC."
    },
